= Isogeny-class rho at 46 bits (replica of P1)
<isogeny-class-rho-at-46-bits-replica-of-p1>
Classification: replication of a null result (rho against rho on one
instrument); not an index-calculus improvement, no leaderboard change,
no claim about any deployed curve.

Protocol: `PROTOCOL.md` (frozen before data, sha256 `f1a2fbd5…6287`),
decision rules R1–R6 inherited from `research/isogeny-class-rho/`. Run:
`runs/run-20261019-n45/` (command card `run.sh`, outputs under `P2/`).
Tool: `src/bin/isoclass_rho` (merged in \#2174).

#strong[Replica at 46 bits: the null holds at 1,773× the group order.]
4,400 class-mode rho solves on 38 isogenous curves of one prime-field
class (P2, `n` \= 46,339,405,405,021), every solve returning the planted
`k`. Pooled mean 1.0097 × √(πn/2) (bootstrap 95% CI 0.993 to 1.026 of
√(πn/2)); Kruskal–Wallis p \= 0.38, ANOVA p \= 0.67, no curve flagged
(max |z| 2.39 against Bonferroni 3.21). The mean ratio P2/P1 is 41.68
against √(n\_P2/n\_P1) \= 42.11 (0.990). Replay reproduces 220/220
iteration counts exactly. #strong[One deviation:] the generators family
(20 generators × 2 vertices) failed the frozen rule (KW p \= 1.2e-4, two
arms flagged); an unplanned fresh-seed repeat written down before
running (`ADDENDUM-generators.md`) did #strong[not] replicate it (KW p
\= 0.97). Both are reported; the first is unexplained.

== What was measured
<what-was-measured>
One class, P2: `F_p`, p \= 46339417407469, a \= 4184642753251, b \=
42214793703111, `#E = n` \= 46,339,405,405,021 (46 bits, prime order).
The walk carries one ECDLP instance by verified isogenies; rho
(32-adding walk, distinguished points, 8 bits) is run on 38 isogenous
curves × 100 seeds, plus 3 isomorphism/representation controls, an A/A
replica, a planted negation fold and a planted 4-adding walk.

